[958.672535, "o", "§151(b) Taxpayer exemption (lines 60-62):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.672549, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[958.672553, "o", "> "]
[958.673179, "o", "\"An exemption of the exemption amount for the taxpayer; and an additional exemption of the exemption amount for the spouse of the taxpayer if a joint return is not made by the taxpayer and his spouse, and if the spouse, for the calendar year in which the taxable year of the taxpayer begins, has no gross income and is not the dependent of another taxpayer.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.673224, "o", "§151(c) Dependents exemption (lines 64-66):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.673477, "o", "\"An exemption of the exemption amount for each individual who is a dependent (as defined in section 152) of the taxpayer for the taxable year.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> §151(d)(3)(A) Phaseout (lines 82-84):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[958.673501, "o", "> "]
[958.673849, "o", "\"In the case of any taxpayer whose adjusted gross income for the taxable year exceeds the applicable amount in effect under section 68(b), the exemption amount shall be reduced by the applicable percentage.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> §151(d)(3)(B) Applicable percentage (lines 86-88):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.673868, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.674301, "o", "\"For purposes of subparagraph (A), the term 'applicable percentage' means 2 percentage points for each $2,500 (or fraction thereof) by which the taxpayer's adjusted gross income for the taxable year exceeds the applicable amount in effect under section 68(b).\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.674334, "o", "§151(b)(2) Basic standard deduction (lines 384-396):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.674506, "o", "\"For purposes of paragraph (1), the basic standard deduction is-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     (C) $3,000 in any other case.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.67454, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.6747, "o", "§68(b)(1)(C) Applicable amount for unmarried (lines 489-490):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.674873, "o", "\"$250,000 in the case of an individual who is not married and who is not a surviving spouse or head of household, and\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> §152(d)(1) Qualifying relative (lines 151-158):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.674905, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.675118, "o", "\"The term 'qualifying relative' means, with respect to any taxpayer for any taxable year, an individual-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.675268, "o", "    (B) who has no income for the calendar year in which such taxable year begins, and\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.675511, "o", "    (D) who is not a qualifying child of such taxpayer or of any other taxpayer for any taxable year beginning in the calendar year in which such taxable year begins.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.675534, "o", "§152(d)(2)(C) Qualifying relative - relationship (lines 167-168):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.675555, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.675723, "o", "\"(C) The father or mother, or an ancestor of either.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Reasoning\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Case facts:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.675757, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.675893, "o", "- Alice's gross income in 2015: $311,510\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Bob (Alice's father) has no income in 2015\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.675936, "o", "- Alice takes the standard deduction in 2015\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.675948, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.676055, "o", "- Alice is unmarried (not married, not surviving spouse, not head of household)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.676065, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.676083, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.67613, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[958.676139, "o", "> "]
[958.676262, "o", "1. Determine filing status: Alice is an unmarried individual under §1(c) (line 29).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.676277, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.676546, "o", "2. Basic standard deduction: Under §151(b)(2)(C) (line 396), the basic standard deduction for \"any other case\" (unmarried) is $3,000.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 3. Personal exemptions:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.676712, "o", "   - Exemption amount under §151(d)(1) (line 72): $2,000 per exemption.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>    - Alice is entitled to one exemption for herself (§151(b)).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.676722, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[958.676731, "o", "> "]
[958.676931, "o", "   - Bob qualifies as Alice's dependent as a qualifying relative under §152(d):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.676964, "o", "     - Relationship test: Bob is Alice's father under §152(d)(2)(C) (line 167).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.677061, "o", "     - Income test: Bob has no income under §152(d)(1)(B) (line 156).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.677074, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.6774, "o", "     - Qualifying child test: Bob cannot be a qualifying child because §152(c)(2)(B) only includes \"child of taxpayer or descendant\" - Bob is Alice's FATHER, not her child.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.677547, "o", "     - Therefore Bob is not a qualifying child under §152(d)(1)(D) (line 157-158).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.677559, "o", "   - Total exemptions before phaseout: 2 × $2,000 = $4,000.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.67757, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.677584, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[958.677597, "o", "> "]
[958.677639, "o", "4. Phaseout calculation (§151(d)(3)):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.677651, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[958.677661, "o", "> "]
[958.677759, "o", "   - Applicable amount for unmarried under §68(b)(1)(C) (line 489): $250,000.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.677771, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.677866, "o", "   - Alice's AGI: $311,510 (gross income equals AGI before exemptions).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.677877, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[958.677883, "o", "> "]
[958.67797, "o", "   - Excess over applicable amount: $311,510 - $250,000 = $61,510.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.677983, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[958.677992, "o", "> "]
[958.678057, "o", "   - Increments of $2,500: ceil($61,510 / $2,500) = 25.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.67807, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.678187, "o", "   - Applicable percentage under §151(d)(3)(B) (line 86): 25 × 2% = 50%.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.678203, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.678304, "o", "   - Reduced exemption amount: $2,000 × (1 - 0.50) = $1,000 per exemption.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.678326, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[958.678461, "o", "> "]
[958.678485, "o", "   - Total exemptions after phaseout: 2 × $1,000 = $2,000.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 5. Taxable income:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.678574, "o", "   - Taxable income = Gross income - Standard deduction - Personal exemptions\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.678593, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.678667, "o", "   - Taxable income = $311,510 - $3,000 - $2,000 = $306,510.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.678682, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.678694, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[958.678704, "o", "> "]
[958.678756, "o", "6. Tax calculation (§1(c)(v) - line 36):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.678768, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[958.67888, "o", "   - For taxable income over $250,000: $79,772 plus 39.6% of excess over $250,000.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.678892, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[958.678904, "o", "> "]
[958.678972, "o", "   - Excess over $250,000: $306,510 - $250,000 = $56,510.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.678982, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[958.678992, "o", "> "]
[958.679098, "o", "   - Tax = $79,772 + (0.396 × $56,510) = $79,772 + $22,377.96 = $102,149.96.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[958.67911, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[958.679119, "o", "> "]
[958.679166, "o", "   - Rounded to whole number: $102,150.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
